  "report": "# R001 mailbox-backpressure: COMPLETED\n\nSeeds: 17, 29, 43, 71, 101. Every seed must hold every coverage and falsifier rule.\n\n- seed 17: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 29: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 43: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 71: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n- seed 101: valid; 0 coverage rules unmet, 0 falsifier rules tripped\n\n- mutation checks of the harness (required for COMPLETED): 27 of 27 killed at 0ac934fe17cbe3037f13fc242653138b4c49e2d0\n- mutations_ok: True\n\nLimitations: scope is ptr_exec::Mailbox and MailboxSender only; the RequestAdmission queue, supervision, restart, cancellation and async mailboxes are not covered; latency is virtual: the gate is wait in simulated ticks against the analytic bound capacity x S_max, not wall-clock time; the threaded arm's wall-clock latency and peak resident set are descriptive and never gated; the threaded arm checks exact counts only (every one of thousands of repeated fills admits exactly the capacity, an Ok after a returned close() is a violation, the ledger holds after the join, a closed mailbox returns every value); how the scheduler interleaves producers is not controlled, so its contended-stage totals vary between runs and are only required to show all three outcomes (admitted, Full, Closed); the model is single-server with uniformly distributed service times and a fixed phase plan; it does not reproduce a real isolate's service distribution, and payload classes differ only in body size; a bounded mailbox that refuses is back-pressure, not delivery: a refused message is returned to the producer, and what the producer does next (retry, shed, escalate) is outside the claim; the reference queue is a VecDeque with a capacity written for this harness; agreement with it shows the Mailbox matches this model, not that the model is the only sound one; negative controls (an unbounded channel, a drop-oldest wrapper) and canaries (duplicating, mutating, lossy, LIFO, capacity+1, capacity x2, early refusal, ignored close, closed reported as empty) show the oracle can tell them from a sound queue; a passing mailbox is the expected outcome; the mutation checker's evidence (results/mutations.json) is about the harness, not the mailbox; COMPLETED requires it (every planned mutation killed) as a precondition of trusting a pass, so without it the verdict is INVALID, and it says nothing about the mailbox itself; wait_bound_violations and payload_bound_violations are corollaries of the capacity, FIFO and model rules and of the harness's own work-conserving consumer (they cannot trip unless those do), and the p99 rule is implied by wait_bound_violations; they are kept because they are the experiment's stated latency and memory claims, not as independent evidence; memory is the queue bound only: the live payload bytes follow from the queue depth; the mailbox's own allocation (the VecDeque buffer) is not gated and appears at most in the descriptive resident set; a panic or a hang of the product is a falsification (product_panics, product_hangs), contained by the harness; a hang is detected only in the threaded arm, by a 20 s watchdog; a panic in harness code itself is a harness fault (INVALID); timings come from one shared cloud container; no capacity claim.\n"
